[180.10682, "o", "a panel on FX revaluation lag chaired by J. Huang. Participants debated whether informal spreadsheets should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 closes that debate for the FY24 extractor.\r\n555:Site visit #299 to treasury exported 12 compliance threads tied to FX revaluation lag. Reviewers noted that effective-date mismatch appeared whenever correction batches straddled a weekend wire cutoff.\r\n559:Interview #698 with treasury counsel captured how FX revaluation lag correspondence referenced amounts near $31,302 without matching ledger rows. Investigators preserved the thread because correction batch ordering can change downstream exception coding.\r\n561:Follow-up #552 confirmed that treasury routed FX revaluation lag statements through a shared inbox with 21 delegates. Investigators flagged retroactive status conflict as the likely root cause of inconsistent status columns.\r\n566:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n568:The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several "]
[180.106827, "o", "notices\r\n569:target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n570:greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n571:`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n572:applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n573:both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n578:## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence — supporting chronology\r\n580:Quality review #167 sampled 23 payroll accrual true-up tickets and found correction batch ordering whenever provisional ledger rows were not filtered before merge.\r\n582:Lead reviewer A. Ndiaye opened working paper WP-8370 after HR finance reported that payroll accrual true-up distorted the May journal reconciliation. The team reconstructed mailbox ordering and found hold flag suppression affecting at least 5 transaction threads.\r\n584:Draft sidebar (non-authoritative): some prototype tooling compared compl"]
[180.107122, "o", "iance mail timestamps against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. Brief 09 later in this archive supersedes that draft practice for production reconciliation.\r\n586:Treasury liaison J. Huang explained that payroll accrual true-up related wires were paused during May journal, delaying compliance responses and amplifying status precedence inversion on rejected rows.\r\n588:Stakeholder workshop #718 on payroll accrual true-up produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.\r\n592:SOX testing team WP-1031 linked retroactive status conflict on payroll accrual true-up to a manual override logged at 02:14 local time between two automated correction imports.\r\n594:Fixed-assets specialist K. Morales argued that payroll accrual true-up capitalization memos should not alter ledger status; investigators agreed while noting those memos still inform exception coding narratives.\r\n596:Audit technologist S. P"]
